  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "php-3-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Righteousness through the faith of Christ, by God. First principle: the two righteousnesses are exclusive — Isaiah's robe is given where law-currency is refused; Paul counts his pedigree as loss for the robe.",
      "density": 2.2536,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-2-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The name above every name is given after the obedience unto death. First principle: Isaiah 52's very high and Psalm 2's decree meet in the wherefore — exaltation is the Father's verdict on the cross.",
      "density": 2.1893,
      "words": 35,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-1-19",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Imprisonment turns to salvation through prayer and Spirit-supply. First principle: Job's hope — I know I shall be justified — is Paul's prison-hope; the Spirit's supply is the deliverance mechanism.",
      "density": 2.1571,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-3-20",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Citizenship in heaven; a Savior awaited. First principle: the colony waits for the Emperor — the Savior from heaven is the coming Lord, and the waiting is civic identity.",
      "density": 2.0393,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-2-15",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Blameless sons of God in a crooked nation. First principle: Deuteronomy 32's crooked generation and Daniel 12's shining wise converge — the church is the light-bearing remnant in the perversity.",
      "density": 2.0071,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-4-19",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Glory-riches in Christ Jesus fund the givers. First principle: the supply follows the sacrifice — the Shepherd-psalm's I shall not want becomes the apostolic promise to a generous church.",
      "density": 1.9821,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-4-18",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Philippians' gift is levitical incense. First principle: giving is sacrifice — the aroma vocabulary of the altar applies to the wallet; well-pleasing gifts smell like the altar.",
      "density": 1.9571,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-2-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The universal confession to the glory of the Father. First principle: Isaiah 45's every-tongue oath is transferred to Jesus — Lord is the covenant name confessed in the covenant oath.",
      "density": 1.95,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-2-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "He humbled Himself and became obedient to death, even the death of the cross. First principle: the lowest point of humiliation is the highest act of love — and the path to exaltation.",
      "density": 1.9107,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-3-21",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The subduing power that raises is the power that rules all things. First principle: resurrection bodies are fashioned like His — the working of enthronement power is aimed at our dust.",
      "density": 1.8607,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-3-3",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "True circumcision is Spirit-worship, Christ-rejoicing, no flesh-confidence. First principle: the uncircumcised heart of Deuteronomy is the true cut — worship in spirit is the covenant's real mark.",
      "density": 1.8179,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-4-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Prayer-peace garrisons hearts and minds in Christ. First principle: the garrison is a sentry of peace — Isaiah's kept-in-perfect-peace mind stands armed at the door of anxiety.",
      "density": 1.8179,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-2-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "At the name of Jesus every knee should bow. First principle: Isaiah's YHWH-claim is applied to Jesus — the most concentrated christological quotation in Paul.",
      "density": 1.6893,
      "words": 25,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-2-7",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The form of a servant, the likeness of men. First principle: kenosis is voluntary descent — the Servant Song's no-form-nor-comeliness and no-place-to-lay-head compressed into one self-emptying.",
      "density": 1.6214,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "php-2-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Who being in the form of God, emptied Himself, taking the form of a servant. First principle: kenosis is not loss of deity but voluntary self-limitation for incarnation and cross.",
      "density": 1.6071,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
